
                                                  CONVERT COMMAND


Coverts supported hex file format into ".hex", ".s19" and ".bin" format.

Below is the syntax :
                 convert 	-in inputFilePath [-igcks {true|false}] -out outputFilePath [-lyt layout]

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -in         |    Input hex file with extension ".hex", ".s19" or ".bin".
   -igcks      |    Ignores wrong line checksum of input hex file when set to TRUE. By default set to FALSE.
               |    Optional switch.
   -out        |    Output hex file path for conversion with appropriate extension of type INTEL(".hex"),
               |    MOTOROLA(".s19") and BIN(".bin").
   -lyt        |    Specifies the layout that the output hex file must be serialized with. Default layout of 0x20.
               |    Optional switch.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	convert -in input.hex -igcks true -out output.s19 -lyt 0x10 
	
